# Dev Preview Sandbox

The Dev Preview Sandbox runs on the VM and is the target for browser validation. It is **not
production and not formal staging** — test data only, no real secrets, no real patient data.

## Topology

- Single-node **k3s**, namespace `impilo-preview`, Helm chart `deploy/helm/impilo-vnext`.
- Components: `experience-bff`, `one-ui-shell`, `postgres`, `redis`, Traefik ingress.
- Public preview URL: `http://41.57.127.235`.
- UI is built **same-origin** (empty `NEXT_PUBLIC_BFF_URL`); the browser calls the BFF via
  relative paths routed by Traefik, so the build is independent of the public IP.

## Authorization

Preview deploy is **manual and user-authorized only**. CI does not deploy after push.
Run `bash scripts/pipeline/run-local-quality-gates.sh` on the VM first, then
`bash scripts/pipeline/cursor-local-feedback.sh` and `bash scripts/ci/collect-ci-feedback.sh`.
Deploy only via `bash scripts/deploy/manual-authorized-preview-deploy.sh` or Actions **Deploy Preview**
after explicit user authorization.

## Deploy → verify loop (run on the VM)

```bash
cd /opt/impilo/repos/Impilo-vNext

# 1. Build before deploy
bash scripts/dev/build-all.sh

# 2. Build images and import into k3s
bash scripts/deploy/preview-build-images.sh

# 3. Deploy via Helm
bash scripts/deploy/preview-deploy.sh

# 4. Confirm pods are healthy
bash scripts/deploy/preview-status.sh
kubectl get pods -n impilo-preview

# 5. Smoke test
bash scripts/deploy/preview-smoke-test.sh

# 6. Logs if needed
bash scripts/deploy/preview-logs.sh experience-bff
bash scripts/deploy/preview-logs.sh one-ui-shell
```

## After every deployment, report

- Preview URL (`http://41.57.127.235`)
- Branch and commit SHA (`git rev-parse --short HEAD`, `curl -s http://41.57.127.235/health/version`)
- Tests run / passed / failed
- Pod health (`kubectl get pods -n impilo-preview`)
- Any blockers

Formal Test/Staging is a separate, future environment — see
`docs/environment/FUTURE_FORMAL_TEST_STAGING_REQUIREMENTS.md`.
